displayxr-runtime (2.66.3-1+stereo3d2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The reason the runtime cannot declare its window to the desktop (the
    desktop announces no stereo declaration, an X11 window the runtime does
    not declare, a build without wayland-scanner) is told to the person
    through sparky-stereo-problems, in the nine languages, and ends when the
    window is declared again; before it reached the log only (Sparky Stereo
    OS ORDER 58b, patch 0009, DXR_SPARKY_PROBLEMS). Depends on
    sparky-stereo-problems (amd64).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 22:50:00 +0000

displayxr-runtime (2.66.3-1+stereo3d1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * DisplayXR 2.66.3 built from its release tag, with displayxr-mcp 0.5.6 and
    displayxr-common 1.2.0 (the two sources its CMake fetches) carried as
    source components, so nothing is downloaded during the build.
  * Three binary packages: the runtime, its dashboard (carried from DisplayXR's
    own release package, checked by SHA-256, since Debian has no .NET), and the
    GNOME Shell window-geometry service under its own publisher name.
  * The runtime joins the openxr1-active-runtime alternatives group that
    Debian's Monado uses, instead of writing the loader's
    /etc/xdg/openxr/1/active_runtime.json itself, so the runtimes installed
    stay selectable side by side.
  * Full side by side for a stereo desktop (Sparky Stereo OS ORDER 34): the
    display processor flag, sim_display's sbs_full output and the declaration
    of the window to Stereo KWin on Wayland and on X11.
  * sim_display is built with XRT_SIM_DISPLAY_FULL_SBS_ONLY: its outputs are 2D
    and full side by side, and Stereo KWin makes every display format from it.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0000
